; grammatical negation — morphological denial of a state or action
; DISTINCT from pratipaksha (semantic opposition):
; pratipaksha: hot ↔ cold — both exist, they oppose semantically
; pratishedha: not-hot — the state is grammatically denied
; 
; in Sanskrit: na, ma, a- prefix (a-satya = not-true)
; in English:  not, no, un-, dis-, without, never, zero
; in extraction: signals prohibition or absence of a quantity

(sangati pratishedha
  (sthita bhasha-swarupa)
  (swarupa viparita)
  (abheda shunya)
  (viparita pratipaksha))
